{"title":"Math circles","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circles</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p><b>Math circles</b> are a growing phenomenon in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_education&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Math education (page does not exist)\">math education</a> around North America.  Inspired by Eastern European teaching models, math circles often take a problem-discussion approach to teaching and learning <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Math_Circles_by_City\">Math Circles by City</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_circles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Math Circles by City\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Albany, NY -- <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Albany_Area_Math_Circle\" title=\"Albany Area Math Circle\">Albany Area Math Circle</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//albanyareamathcircle.blogspot.com/\">Home</a></li>\n<li>Ann Arbor, MI -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.math.lsa.umich.edu/mathcircle/\">Michigan Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Atlanta, GA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.mathcs.emory.edu/mathcircle/\">Emory Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Boston, MA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.msri.org/communications/vmath/VMathVideos/VideoInfo/1913/show_video\">Boston Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Boston, MA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.themathcircle.org/\">The Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Columbia, MD -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//chesapeakemath.catherineasaro.net\">Chesapeake Math Program</a></li>\n<li>Dallas, TX -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.metroplexmathcircle.org/\">Metroplex Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Davis, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.math.ucdavis.edu/~exploration/mathcircle/\">Davis Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Long Beach, CA -- <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Southern_California_ARML\" title=\"Southern California ARML\">Southern California ARML</a></li>\n<li>Los Angeles, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.math.ucla.edu/~radko/circles/\">Los Angeles Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Miami, FL -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.fiu.edu/~draghici/mathcircle_files/mathcircle.html\">Miami Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Mobile, AL -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.southalabama.edu/mathstat/non-css-mathcircle.shtml\">Mobile Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>New Hampshire -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//nhmath.org\">New Hampshire Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>New York City, NY -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//comet.lehman.cuny.edu/mathcircle/\">Lehman College Math Circle</a> (in the Bronx)</li>\n<li>New York City, NY -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.nymathcircle.org/\">New York Math Circle</a> (at NYU)</li>\n<li>Orlando, FL -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.orlandomathcircle.org/\">Orlando Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Palo Alto, CA -- Gunn Math Circle, along with its respective competition <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gunn_Math_Competition_(GMC)\" title=\"Gunn Math Competition (GMC)\">Gunn Math Competition (GMC)</a></li>\n<li>Palo Alto, CA -- <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stanford_Math_Circle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Stanford Math Circle (page does not exist)\">Stanford Math Circle</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.stanfordmathcircle.org/\">Home</a></li>\n<li>Salt Lake City, Utah -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.math.utah.edu/mathcircle/\">Utah Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Santa Barbara, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//santabarbaramathellipse.org/\">Santa Barbara Math Ellipse</a></li>\n<li>San Diego, CA -- <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=San_Diego_Math_Circle\" title=\"San Diego Math Circle\">San Diego Math Circle</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.artofproblemsolving.com/SDMC/AoPS_S_About.php\">Home</a></li>\n<li>San Francisco, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//mathcircle.berkeley.edu/\">Berkeley Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>San Francisco, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.castilleja.org/faculty/josh_zucker/gunn/bamo/circles/GunnHS/index.html\">Gunn HS Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>San Francisco, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.sfmathcircle.org/\">San Francisco Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>San Jose, CA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.geometer.org/sjcircle/\">San Jose Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Seattle, WA -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//sites.math.washington.edu/~mathcircle/circle/\">UW Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Toronto (Canada) -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.torontomathcircles.ca/\">Toronto Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Waterloo (Canada) -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.cemc.uwaterloo.ca/~mathcirc/\">Waterloo Math Circle</a></li>\n<li>Wyoming -- <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//uwacadweb.uwyo.edu/UW_MATH_CIRCLE/\">Wyoming Math Circle</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_circles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">Math books</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">Mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_problem_solving\" title=\"Mathematical problem solving\">Mathematical problem solving</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"External_Links\">External Links</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_circles&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: External Links\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving_Foundation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving Foundation\">Art of Problem Solving Foundation</a> runs a local programs initiative to support the establishment of programs including the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=San_Diego_Math_Circle\" title=\"San Diego Math Circle\">San Diego Math Circle</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.geometer.org/mathcircles/\">Tom Davis notes on math circle lessons</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200140\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.108 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 28/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 84/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 46/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.705      1 Template:Distinguish\n100.00%   15.705      1 -total\n 48.07%    7.550      1 Template:Hatnote\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1468:|#|:idhash:canonic